The language packs (packs/*.json, packs/*.pairs.bin) are built by lab/build.py, lab/build_docmodel.py,
lab/tune_doc.py and lab/bench.py. They hold aggregate statistics only: rates and ratios of words, word sequences,
word pairs and sentence templates, word forms and parts of speech, model parameters and score percentiles. No
document text is included. The statistics are derived from the corpora and data below; each is used under the
terms its publisher states.

Human text written before 2022-11-30
  - Leipzig Corpora Collection (news, Wikipedia and web corpora), Leipzig University.
    https://wortschatz.uni-leipzig.de - terms of use as published there.
  - FineWeb and FineWeb-2, Hugging Face (HuggingFaceFW/fineweb, HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-2).
    Open Data Commons Attribution License (ODC-By) v1.0; subject to the Common Crawl terms of use.
  - Stack Overflow posts from the Stack Exchange data dump (mikex86/stackoverflow-posts,
    IlyaGusev/ru_stackoverflow). User contributions licensed under CC BY-SA (2.5, 3.0 or 4.0, depending on
    when the post was written); the IlyaGusev/ru_stackoverflow card states CC BY-SA 2.5 for that dataset.
  - The Pile (EleutherAI), uncopyrighted subset (monology/pile-uncopyrighted). The dataset card states the
    license as "other"; the licenses of the components vary, see The Pile paper (arXiv:2101.00027).
  - Pikabu posts and comments (IlyaGusev/pikabu). No license is stated on the dataset card.
  - wordfreq, Robyn Speer. Code under the Apache License 2.0, data under CC BY-SA 4.0.

LLM text, and the human texts paired with it in LLMTrace, HAP-E and SAGE (document style models, benchmark)
  - LLMTrace (iitolstykh/LLMTrace_classification). Apache License 2.0.
  - HAP-E, the Human-AI Parallel English corpus (browndw/human-ai-parallel-corpus). MIT License.
  - SAGE (EndLessTime/SAGE). No license is stated on the dataset card.
  - WildChat-4.8M (allenai/WildChat-4.8M), Allen Institute for AI. Open Data Commons Attribution License
    (ODC-By) v1.0.

Lemmatization (the word form and part-of-speech tables in the packs)
  - simplemma, Adrien Barbaresi. MIT License. Its lemmatization data come from several sources, among them the
    Lemmatization lists by Michal Měchura (Open Database License) and the Wikinflection corpus by Eleni
    Metheniti (CC BY 4.0); see the simplemma credits.
  - pymorphy3 (MIT License) with the pymorphy3-dicts-ru dictionaries, compiled from OpenCorpora
    (https://opencorpora.org). Dictionary data under CC BY-SA 3.0.

Attribution under ODC-By: the packs are Produced Works that contain content obtained from FineWeb, FineWeb-2 and
WildChat-4.8M. Those databases are available under the Open Data Commons Attribution License v1.0,
